                      (        ccide.asm):00001         ********************************************************************
                      (        ccide.asm):00002         * CCIDE - IDE device driver for CoCo
                      (        ccide.asm):00003         *
                      (        ccide.asm):00004         * DO NOT FORGET TO SET H6309 FLAG IN DEFSFILE APPROPRIATELY FOR 6809 VS.
                      (        ccide.asm):00005         *   6309 CODE WHEN ASSEMBLING!!
                      (        ccide.asm):00006         *
                      (        ccide.asm):00007         *  Driver originally from Jim Hathaway, originally 8-bit only
                      (        ccide.asm):00008         *  Converted to 16 bit by Alan DeKok
                      (        ccide.asm):00009         *  Disassembled (OK, so I didn't have the source version at first!)
                      (        ccide.asm):00010         *     by Eddie Kuns, ATA specs followed carefully and sector buffering
                      (        ccide.asm):00011         *     on writes handled more carefully
                      (        ccide.asm):00012         * This driver uses 16-bit transfers *only*
                      (        ccide.asm):00013         * Check with Glenside - can we switch to 16 bit only, so there is less to
                      (        ccide.asm):00014         *   maintain? With the cacheing stuff, the speed is fairly decent, although
                      (        ccide.asm):00015         *   some 6309 optimizations are still possible (cache copies, drive table
                      (        ccide.asm):00016         *   copies, hardware divide for CHS translation, etc.)
                      (        ccide.asm):00017         *
                      (        ccide.asm):00018         * NOTE: Currently, will return RAW error #'s from drive (see ATA bit flags
                      (        ccide.asm):00019         *   in error register). After driver finalized, switch back to OS9 error
                      (        ccide.asm):00020         *   codes.
                      (        ccide.asm):00021         * NOTE 2: drvrbusy checks are done even before hardware access, because
                      (        ccide.asm):00022         *  some variables are shared in the driver memory, and if a 2nd request
                      (        ccide.asm):00023         *  comes in in the middle of it, the vars might be changed at a dangerous
                      (        ccide.asm):00024         *  time. Note if you have two IDE controllers: since they get separate driver
                      (        ccide.asm):00025         *  memory from each other, that both controllers CAN be active at the same
                      (        ccide.asm):00026         *  time.
                      (        ccide.asm):00027         * BIG NOTE ON OLDER ATA-1 DRIVES!!!
                      (        ccide.asm):00028         * SOME DRIVES (MY MINISCRIBE 8051A INCLUDED) HAVE A TRANSLATION MODE THAT
                      (        ccide.asm):00029         * _IS_BUILT_INTO_THE_IDE_ROM_ITSELF! THE BAD PART IS, THE "IDENTIFY DRIVE"
                      (        ccide.asm):00030         * COMMAND _DOES_NOT_ TAKE THIS INTO CONSIDERATION, BUT RETURNS THE "NATIVE"
                      (        ccide.asm):00031         * DRIVE SPECS FOR CYLINDERS, HEADS & SECTORS PER TRACK. TO GET THE FULL
                      (        ccide.asm):00032         * CAPACITY OF THE DRIVE, WITHOUT ERRORS, YOU _MUST_ SET YOUR DEVICE
                      (        ccide.asm):00033         * DESCRIPTOR BASED ON THE HARDWARE _TRANSLATED_ SETTINGS, _NOT_ THE _NATIVE_
                      (        ccide.asm):00034         * SETTINGS (DESCRIBED IN THE IDENTIFY DRIVE COMMAND)! AS A REAL WORLD
                      (        ccide.asm):00035         * EXAMPLE, ON MY MINISCRIBE 8051A:
                      (        ccide.asm):00036         *   Drives "Native"  mode (as well as the Identify Drive command) returns:
                      (        ccide.asm):00037         *     745 cylinders, 4 heads & 28 sectors/cylinder.
                      (        ccide.asm):00038         *  HOWEVER, the "Translation" mode (which is checked off on the sticker on
                      (        ccide.asm):00039         *    the drive itself from the manufacturer), says:
                      (        ccide.asm):00040         *    Translated: 5 heads, 17 sectors. At this point, you will have to figure
                      (        ccide.asm):00041         *      out the # of cylinders, by computing the # of sectors TOTAL for the
                      (        ccide.asm):00042         *      drive in it's native mode (745*4*28 in the above example, or 83,440
                      (        ccide.asm):00043         *      sectors), and then dividing that value by (# of sectors/track * # of
                      (        ccide.asm):00044         *      heads) in the translation mode, and rounding down. In the above case,
                      (        ccide.asm):00045         *      83,440/(5*17)=981.647, so use 981 (which in hex is $03d5).
                      (        ccide.asm):00046         * Therefore, the proper device descriptor for this drive is:
                      (        ccide.asm):00047         *  cyl=3d5 sid=5 sct=22 t0s=22  (Actually, t0s is ignored by CCIDE)
                      (        ccide.asm):00048         *    The sct=22 is because the value is hexidecimal (it means 34 sectors/
                      (        ccide.asm):00049         *    track), and is double the 17 I mentioned above because OS9 sectors are
                      (        ccide.asm):00050         *    half the size of IDE sectors (256 bytes vs. 512 bytes). If this drive
                      (        ccide.asm):00051         *    had been shipped in "Native" mode, it would use the following:
                      (        ccide.asm):00052         *  cyl=2E9 sid=4 sct=38 t0s=38, which is what the IDENTIFY DRIVE command
                      (        ccide.asm):00053         *    reports.
                      (        ccide.asm):00054         * You can verify the highest cylinder # by setting the OFS in the descriptor
                      (        ccide.asm):00055         *   to what you think is the highest cylinder # (total # of cylinders-1 ...
                      (        ccide.asm):00056         *   remember that CHS cylinder numbers start at 0!), and then try to read
                      (        ccide.asm):00057         *   enough sectors to cover the whole track. If you go one past that value,
                      (        ccide.asm):00058         *   you should start getting errors if you have the right cylinder count.
                      (        ccide.asm):00059         * This is kind of a dumb system, but I assume it had something to do with
                      (        ccide.asm):00060         * IBM PC BIOS in the early days of IDE.
                      (        ccide.asm):00061         *A LITTLE LATER, WHEN THE DRIVER IS STABLE, MAY WANT TO ADD ANOTHER BIT FLAG
                      (        ccide.asm):00062         *  TO DRIVEFLG, SET UP BY A FIRST TIME READ: 8 BIT ACCEPTED. THEN, USE THE 8
                      (        ccide.asm):00063         *  BIT TRANSFER MODE IF POSSIBLE (LIKE I DID WITH LBA). THIS SHOULD ALLOW
                      (        ccide.asm):00064         *  MUCH FASTER SECTOR ACCESS ON A NITROS9 SYSTEM, AND IT WOULD BE INTERESTING
                      (        ccide.asm):00065         *  TO SEE HOW MANY DRIVES ACCEPT THAT MODE (SUPPOSED TO RETURN AN 'ABORTED'
                      (        ccide.asm):00066         *  FLAG IF IT DOES NOT).
                      (        ccide.asm):00067         * NOTE: RBF WILL ASSIGN NEW DEVICE MEM (,U PTR) TO _EACH_ CONTROLLER ON IT'S
                      (        ccide.asm):00068         *   OWN, BASED ON THE BASE ADDRESS FROM THE DEVICE DESCRIPTOR. THEREFORE,
                      (        ccide.asm):00069         *   CCIDE SHOULD BE SET UP FOR _2_ DRIVES MAX (PER CONTROLLER), AND LET RBF
                      (        ccide.asm):00070         *   TAKE CARE OF MULTIPLE CONTROLLERS.
                      (        ccide.asm):00071         *    The exception to this is when using partitions; since they will have a
                      (        ccide.asm):00072         *    separate descriptor for each partition, they will need a separate drive
                      (        ccide.asm):00073         *    table entry. Each table entry is $26 (38) bytes each, so it is not a lot.
                      (        ccide.asm):00074         *    Should make the device table fill up the rest of a 256 byte page (with
                      (        ccide.asm):00075         *    all other variables allocated), since OS9 will force System RAM pages to
                      (        ccide.asm):00076         *    even multiples of 256 anyways. Once full 8k block caching is implemented,
                      (        ccide.asm):00077         *    some of the two 256 byte sector buffers currently in system RAM could be
                      (        ccide.asm):00078         *    reused for more drive table entries as well. With current system RAM
                      (        ccide.asm):00079         *    requirements in driver, this would allow 5 device table entries without
                      (        ccide.asm):00080         *    taking any more system RAM then it is already. These can be shared in
                      (        ccide.asm):00081         *    whatever combination you need for your (up to) 2 physical drives.
                      (        ccide.asm):00082         * ALSO, RBF CALLS THE INIT ROUTINE ONLY ONCE PER _DRIVER_, NOT DRIVE!
                      (        ccide.asm):00083         *
                      (        ccide.asm):00084         * Ed.    Comments                                       Who YY/MM/DD
                      (        ccide.asm):00085         * ------------------------------------------------------------------
                      (        ccide.asm):00086         * 5      Source as distributed by Glenside                  99/05/02
                      (        ccide.asm):00087         *        Added comments from 8 bit driver               BGP 99/05/07
                      (        ccide.asm):00088         * 6      Driver now gets address from descriptor, made  BGP 99/05/10
                      (        ccide.asm):00089         *        minor optimizations, added symbols
                      (        ccide.asm):00090         * 7      Change to use real 16 bits                     LCB 99/09/06
                      (        ccide.asm):00091         *        partitions (both LBA & CHS)                     to 99/10/31
                      (        ccide.asm):00092         *        better error reporting
                      (        ccide.asm):00093         *        slightly optimized read
                      (        ccide.asm):00094         *        Half sector & LSN0 caches for current drive
                      (        ccide.asm):00095         *        Auto-sense/run LBA & CHS modes
                      (        ccide.asm):00096         *        Full CHS calculations (up to 4096 cylinders)
                      (        ccide.asm):00097         *          for ATA-1 old drive compatibility
                      (        ccide.asm):00098         * 8      Attempted to add support for removable media   LCB 00/05/27
                      (        ccide.asm):00099         *         commands (Door Lock/Unlock, Acknowledge Media  to 00/??/??
                      (        ccide.asm):00100         *         Change)
                      (        ccide.asm):00101         *        Attempt 'generic' ATA command system call
                      (        ccide.asm):00102         * Constants - change if needed
                      (        ccide.asm):00103         * NUMDRIVE is LOGICAL drives (partitions), NOT physical drives-use 5,11,etc
                      (        ccide.asm):00104         * 5=768 byte data area, 11=1024 byte data area
     000B             (        ccide.asm):00105         NUMDRIVE            equ       11                  Max. # of device descriptors per controller address
     012C             (        ccide.asm):00106         MAXWAIT             equ       60*5                Max. # clock ticks to give up on read/write (5 sec)
     0800             (        ccide.asm):00107         HDSclPwr            equ       2048                Set to 2048 as start ^2 cylinder (CHS translate)
                      (        ccide.asm):00108         
                      (        ccide.asm):00109         * New definitions in Device Descriptor
     0026             (        ccide.asm):00110         PartOfs             equ       $26                 2 byte partition offset
                      (        ccide.asm):00111         
                      (        ccide.asm):00112         * Definitions for DD.DNS
     0001             (        ccide.asm):00113         PhysDriv            equ       %00000001           Physical drive # (0=Master, 1=Slave)
     0002             (        ccide.asm):00114         ForceCHS            equ       %00000010           Force driver to use CHS mode
                      (        ccide.asm):00115         
                      (        ccide.asm):00116         * New GetStat/SetStat calls:
                      (        ccide.asm):00117         * SS.DrInf call shares call # with SS.ScInf from NitrOS9 WindInt (info)
     008F             (        ccide.asm):00118         SS.DrInf            equ       $8f                 Drive info call (see routine for parms)
                      (        ccide.asm):00119         * Subcall #'s fro SS.DrInf (Y register on entry)
     0000             (        ccide.asm):00120         ATAIdent            equ       0                   ATA (handles ATAPI & plain ATA)
                      (        ccide.asm):00121         
                      (        ccide.asm):00122         * IDE & ATAPI Commands (ATAPI stuff not implemented yet, and LBA is mandatory)
     0020             (        ccide.asm):00123         ReadRtry            equ       $20                 Read sector with retry
     0030             (        ccide.asm):00124         WritRtry            equ       $30                 Write sector with retry
     0090             (        ccide.asm):00125         Diagnost            equ       $90                 Execute drive diagnostic
     00EC             (        ccide.asm):00126         Identify            equ       $EC                 Identify drive command
     00DE             (        ccide.asm):00127         DoorLock            equ       $DE                 Lock drive
     00DF             (        ccide.asm):00128         DoorUnLk            equ       $DF                 Unlock (eject) drive
     00DB             (        ccide.asm):00129         AckMdChg            equ       $DB                 Acknowledge media change
                      (        ccide.asm):00130         
     00A1             (        ccide.asm):00131         PIIdent             equ       $A1                 Identify ATAPI drive command
                      (        ccide.asm):00132         
                      (        ccide.asm):00133         * IDE Status Register
     0080             (        ccide.asm):00134         Busy                equ       %10000000           Drive busy (1=busy)
     0040             (        ccide.asm):00135         DrvReady            equ       %01000000           Drive ready (1=ready to accept command)
     0020             (        ccide.asm):00136         WriteFlt            equ       %00100000           Drive Write Fault (1=Write fault?)
     0010             (        ccide.asm):00137         SeekDone            equ       %00010000           Seek Complete (1=Seek complete)
     0008             (        ccide.asm):00138         DataReq             equ       %00001000           Data Request (1=drive ready for read/write data)
     0004             (        ccide.asm):00139         CorrData            equ       %00000100           Corrected Data (1=correctable data error was done)
     0002             (        ccide.asm):00140         Index               equ       %00000010           1=1 disk revolution completed
     0001             (        ccide.asm):00141         ErrorFnd            equ       %00000001           1=Error detected - see error register
                      (        ccide.asm):00142         
                      (        ccide.asm):00143         * IDE hardware offsets
     0000             (        ccide.asm):00144         DataReg             equ       0                   Data (1st 8 bits, non-latched)
     0001             (        ccide.asm):00145         Error               equ       1                   Error # when read
     0001             (        ccide.asm):00146         Features            equ       1                   Features when write
     0002             (        ccide.asm):00147         SectCnt             equ       2                   Sector count
     0003             (        ccide.asm):00148         SectNum             equ       3                   Sector #
     0004             (        ccide.asm):00149         CylLow              equ       4                   Low byte of cylinder
     0005             (        ccide.asm):00150         CylHigh             equ       5                   High byte of cylinder
     0006             (        ccide.asm):00151         DevHead             equ       6                   Device/Head
     0007             (        ccide.asm):00152         Status              equ       7                   Status when read
     0007             (        ccide.asm):00153         Command             equ       7                   Command when write
     0008             (        ccide.asm):00154         Latch               equ       8                   Latch (2nd 8 bits of 16 bit word)
                      (        ccide.asm):00155         
                      (        ccide.asm):00156         * Special flags (Mini extra drive table - 1 byte per drive) - starts at
                      (        ccide.asm):00157         *    DriveFlg,u
                      (        ccide.asm):00158         * These are set by inquiring the drive, NOT from the descriptor
                      (        ccide.asm):00159         * Should add a GETSTAT to allow user to access these for any drive
     0080             (        ccide.asm):00160         Unused              equ       %10000000           Entry is un-initialized
     0001             (        ccide.asm):00161         DrvMode             equ       %00000001           0=CHS mode, 1=LBA mode
     0002             (        ccide.asm):00162         ATAPI               equ       %00000010           0=Device is ATA,1=Device is ATAPI
     0004             (        ccide.asm):00163         Remove              equ       %00000100           0=Fixed Drive, 1=Removable media
     0008             (        ccide.asm):00164         ReadOnly            equ       %00001000           0=Read & write allowed, 1=Read only (CD-ROM)
                      (        ccide.asm):00165         *                           Could also use to write-protect hard drive
                      (        ccide.asm):00166                             nam       CCIDE
                      (        ccide.asm):00167                             ttl       IDE device driver for CoCo
                      (        ccide.asm):00168         
                      (        ccide.asm):00169                             ifp1
                      (        ccide.asm):00170                             use       defsfile
                      (         defsfile):00001             use os9.d
                      (            os9.d):00001                             IFNE      OS9.D-1
                      (            os9.d):00002         
     0001             (            os9.d):00003         OS9.D               SET       1
